Verified against live CreateOS, not just unit tests.

Engine e2e (3 real sandboxes): staged dir visible in box, artifact pulled
back to host, box confirmed destroyed via the API, egress restriction
applied, real exit code surfaced. 14/14.

Bug found and fixed by that e2e, invisible to unit tests: pullArtifacts
reported success for a pull that never happened. GNU tar writes a
well-formed EMPTY archive when asked for a missing path and reports the
failure only in its exit status, so the receiving tar succeeds and a
/bin/sh pipeline — whose status is the last command's — exits 0. The box
holding the only copy of the output was then destroyed. cos was never
affected (set -euo pipefail); the port lost that property through
execSync, which defaults to /bin/sh. Fixed at execShell plus an explicit
existence probe.

Retention and egress are pure functions specifically so they can be
tested without a sandbox.
